These fixtures exercise the MAC capability keystore and channel protocols.
They are not selected by sys/modules, buildkernel, buildworld or test installation.

In a source checkout, build for the kernel used by the isolated test VM:
  make -j$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu) -C tests/sys/mac_capability fixtures KERNBUILDDIR=/path/to/kernel/objects
The normal /usr/obj object root is used. Determine the fixture object root with:
  make -C tests/sys/mac_capability/fixtures -V .OBJDIR
Copy its kernelstore/ and keystore/ .ko files to the isolated test VM, preserving
those subdirectories, and set MAC_CAPABILITY_FIXTURE_DIR to their parent when
running run_tests.sh. Do not load fixtures on the production capability plane.
The runner's existing plane-free and root requirements still apply.

The matching protocol headers live in fixtures/include. Tests and fixture
modules consume the same definitions. Production code does not include them.
